{
  "kind": "lesson",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "brighter-lamp",
  "packId": "lawp.circuits.basics",
  "courseId": "resistance",
  "moduleId": "experiment",
  "title": "Make the lamp brighter",
  "skillIds": [
    "circuits.series.current"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 8,
  "taskRev": 1,
  "creation": {
    "id": "my-circuit",
    "step": 1,
    "briefMd": "Tune the lamp without breaking the current cap."
  },
  "mastery": {
    "requiresTransfer": true,
    "minCorrectIndependent": 1
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "id": "brighter-lamp",
      "kind": "experiment",
      "engine": "world-v1",
      "promptMd": "Make the lamp brighter without letting current go above 2.",
      "skillIds": [
        "circuits.series.current"
      ],
      "constraintMode": "final",
      "predict": {
        "promptMd": "If you lower resistance, what happens to current?",
        "kind": "mcq",
        "choices": [
          {
            "id": "up",
            "md": "Current rises"
          },
          {
            "id": "down",
            "md": "Current falls",
            "misconceptionId": "ignores-current-limit"
          },
          {
            "id": "same",
            "md": "Current stays the same"
          }
        ],
        "answer": "up"
      },
      "world": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "id": "battery",
            "type": "battery",
            "props": {
              "cells": 1
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "resistor",
            "type": "resistor",
            "props": {
              "ohms": 2
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "lamp",
            "type": "lamp",
            "props": {
              "brightness": 1,
              "label": "Lamp"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "meter",
            "type": "meter",
            "props": {
              "current": 0.5
            }
          }
        ],
        "connections": [
          {
            "from": "battery",
            "to": "resistor"
          },
          {
            "from": "resistor",
            "to": "lamp"
          },
          {
            "from": "lamp",
            "to": "battery"
          }
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "id": "set-ohms",
            "label": "Set resistance",
            "target": "resistor",
            "op": "set",
            "key": "ohms",
            "values": [
              0,
              0.25,
              1,
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ],
        "rules": [
          {
            "id": "i-from-lookup",
            "when": [],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "meter",
                "key": "current",
                "value": {
                  "op": "div",
                  "a": "battery.cells",
                  "b": "resistor.ohms"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "bright-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "gte",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "dim-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "lt",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "view": {
          "kind": "graph",
          "assetMap": {
            "lamp@brightness=1": "assets/lamp-dim.svg",
            "lamp@brightness=2": "assets/lamp-bright.svg",
            "battery": "assets/battery.svg",
            "resistor": "assets/resistor.svg",
            "meter": "assets/meter.svg"
          }
        }
      },
      "goal": {
        "all": [
          {
            "path": "lamp.brightness",
            "op": "eq",
            "value": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        {
          "path": "meter.current",
          "op": "lte",
          "value": 2
        }
      ],
      "explainAfter": {
        "promptMd": "Why did brightness change? Current is cells ÷ resistance. Too little resistance and current overshoots the safe cap."
      },
      "misconceptionMap": [
        {
          "when": {
            "path": "meter.current",
            "op": "gt",
            "value": 2
          },
          "misconceptionId": "ignores-current-limit"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Look at the meter, not only the lamp."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Current ≈ cells / ohms. One cell. Cap is 2."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Try ohms = 1. Avoid 0.25 if you want to stay under the cap."
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "Set resistance to 1, then Check."
        },
        {
          "level": 5,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "ohms=1 → current=1 → brightness=2 and 1 ≤ 2."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Brightness follows current, and current has a ceiling\n\nYou just moved one knob and watched two things answer. Resistance went down, current went up, and the lamp got brighter. That chain is the whole lesson: **current is cells ÷ resistance**, and **brightness follows current**. You never set brightness directly. You set the squeeze, and the loop works out the rest.\n\n![A lamp shining brightly in a closed loop](assets/lamp-bright.svg)\n\nRun the knob you were given through that chain and the cap decides for you:\n\n```text\nresistance  current = 1 cell / ohms   lamp        cap of 2\n4           0.25                      dim         ok\n2           0.5                       dim         ok\n1           1                         bright      ok\n0.25        4                         too much    OVER\n```\n\nThe trap is thinking brighter is always better, so less resistance is always better. It is not. Every real part has a current it can survive, and this lamp's ceiling was 2. Drop the resistance to 0.25 and the current climbs to 4 — twice what the part can take. On the bench that is not a brighter lamp, it is a dead one, and a very hot resistor on the way out.\n\nSo the goal was never \"maximum current\". It was the **brightest lamp that still obeys the cap** — resistance 1, current 1, comfortably under 2. Aiming at the biggest number instead of the best number is how beginners let the smoke out.\n\nNext you will look at where that ceiling comes from in the first place."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Predict what will happen, then change the circuit so the lamp shines brighter."
}
